            600
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-1",
        "path": "media/korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-1-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of hands lowering lid onto saucepan of jasmine rice",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2",
      "number": 2,
      "heading": "Pickle the carrot",
      "blocks": [
        "Peel the carrot into ribbons, stopping at the core. Mix rice vinegar, {{pickle-sugar}} sugar and salt, toss with the ribbons and set aside. Trim and separate pak choi leaves and halve the large ones lengthways. Peel and grate the garlic."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [],
      "image": {
        "id": "korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-2",
        "path": "media/korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-2-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of pak choi and carrot ribbons on board",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3",
      "number": 3,
      "heading": "Fry the steaks",
      "blocks": [
        "Heat oil on high. Season steaks and fry 6–8 minutes for medium rare depending on thickness, turning halfway. Cook longer for your preferred doneness. Rest under foil for a couple of minutes. Wash hands and equipment after handling raw meat."
      ],
      "notes": [
        "For more well-done steak, add about 1 minute on each side."
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Fry the steaks",
          "seconds": [
            360,
            480
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-3",
        "path": "media/korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-3-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of two rump steaks frying",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4",
      "number": 4,
      "heading": "Fry the pak choi",
      "blocks": [
        "Return the pan to high heat with oil. Stir-fry pak choi for 3–4 minutes until just soft, add garlic and stir-fry for 30 seconds. Season and keep warm in a covered bowl."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Fry the pak choi",
          "seconds": [
            180,
            240
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-4",
        "path": "media/korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-4-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of pak choi in frying pan",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-5",
      "number": 5,
      "heading": "Make the sauce",
      "blocks": [
        "Put the pan back over medium heat and stir in gochujang, bulgogi sauce and {{sauce-water}} water. Bring to a boil, then simmer 1–2 minutes until thickened. Use less gochujang for a milder sauce and loosen with water if needed."
      ],
      "notes": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "id": "timer-1",
          "label": "Make the sauce",
          "seconds": [
            60,
            120
          ]
        }
      ],
      "image": {
        "id": "korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-5",
        "path": "media/korean-rump-steak-bibimbap-5-sketch.webp",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 480,
        "alt": "Sketch of dark bulgogi gochujang sauce in pan",
        "credit": "Illustration based on the HelloFresh recipe card"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "step-6",
      "number": 6,
      "heading": "Serve",
      "blocks": [
        "Pour the carrot pickling liquid into the rice and fluff with a fork. Divide rice into bowls and arrange sliced steak, pak choi and carrot separately. Spoon sauce over the steak, drizzle over {{mayo}} mayonnaise and scatter with sesame."
      ],
      "notes": [],
